.* ASSIST: the task menu for the operational assistant.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='ASSIST'.
:IMPORT NAME=CHGPWD PNLGRP=QHSYCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=SIGNOFF PNLGRP=QHWMCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=SNDMSG PNLGRP=QHMHCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKMSG PNLGRP=QHMHCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKSPLF PNLGRP=QHSPCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKUSRJOB PNLGRP=QHWMCMD.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/MENUKEYS' NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.F1=Help
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION='CMD CALL QCMD'.F9=Command line
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=ASSIST HELP=HLPASSIST KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Operational Assistant (TM) Menu
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.To select one of the following, type its number below and press Enter:
:MENUI HELP=WRKSPLF OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD WRKSPLF'.Work with printer output
:MENUI HELP=WRKUSRJOB OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD WRKUSRJOB'.Work with jobs
:MENUI HELP=WRKMSG OPTION=3 ACTION='CMD WRKMSG'.Work with messages
:MENUI HELP=SNDMSG OPTION=4 ACTION='CMD ?SNDMSG'.Send messages
:MENUI HELP=CHGPWD OPTION=5 ACTION='CMD CHGPWD'.Change your password
:MENUI HELP='ASSIST/OPT10' OPTION=10 ACTION='MENU MANAGESYS'.Manage your system, users, and devices
:MENUI HELP='ASSIST/OPT11' OPTION=11 ACTION='MENU SETUP'.Customize your system, users, and devices
:MENUI HELP='ASSIST/OPT75' OPTION=75 ACTION='MENU USERHELP'.Information and problem handling
:MENUI HELP=SIGNOFF OPTION=80 ACTION='CMD SIGNOFF'.Temporary sign-off
:EMENU.
:BOTINST.Type a menu option below
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPASSIST.Operational Assistant (TM) Menu - Help
:P.A short list of the tasks most users need, without a command line. F9
opens one when a command is wanted.
:P.Type an option number and press Enter. F9 opens a command line, F3
leaves the menu and F12 returns to the one before it.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F1=Help
:PD.Shows help for where the cursor is.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F9=Command line
:PD.Shows a command line to run a command from.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ASSIST/OPT10'.Manage your system, users, and devices
:P.Option 10. Shows menu MANAGESYS&colon. Manage your system, users, and
devices.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ASSIST/OPT11'.Customize your system, users, and devices
:P.Option 11. Shows menu SETUP&colon. Customize your system, users, and
devices.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ASSIST/OPT75'.Information and problem handling
:P.Option 75. Shows menu USERHELP&colon. Information and problem
handling.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
